There are several files here and several directories, most with historical importance (for different articles).

Current versions:
apr_ocl_num_int_el_reference_prism_QSS.cl  
apr_ocl_num_int_el_reference_tetra_QSS.cl 
apr_ocl_num_int_el_reference_prism_SQS.cl  
apr_ocl_num_int_el_reference_tetra_SQS.cl 
apr_ocl_num_int_el_reference_prism_SSQ.cl  
apr_ocl_num_int_el_reference_tetra_SSQ.cl

All six were tested for conv_diff_prism_std codes and test_scalar problem.

Switches (with #define):

Group one - MUST BE COMPATIBLE WITH utd_util/opencl/uts_ls_intf_opencl.c!!!!!
0. Master switch: GPU versus PHI versus CPU
//#define CPU_OPENCL
//#define GPU_OPENCL
//#define PHI_OPENCL
1. #define SCALAR - float versus double 
   !!! has to be switched accordingly to utd_util/opencl/uts_ls_intf_opencl.c !!!
2. #define JACOBIAN_CALCULATIONS_GPU - entries for Jacobian matrices not computed
   based on geometry of elements, but read directly from input files
   !!! has to be switched accordingly to utd_util/opencl/uts_ls_intf_opencl.c !!!
3. #define LAPLACE - kernels can be used for Laplace equations 
   #define TEST_NUM_INT - or for a testing example 
   solved by conv_diff_prism_std codes (e.g. diff_in_box problems)
   !!! has to be switched accordingly to utd_util/opencl/uts_ls_intf_opencl.c !!!
4. #define WORK_GROUP_SIZE_MAX 64/16/8 - assumed work-group size
   !!! has to be switched accordingly to utd_util/opencl/uts_ls_intf_opencl.c !!!

Group two - for kernel use only




